    oeq:q_diabetic_nephropathy_treatment oe:answerText "Limited evidence exists to support the simultaneous initiation of sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitors and finerenone, a nonsteroidal mineralocorticoid receptor antagonist, in persons with chronic kidney disease and type 2 diabetes. We randomly assigned participants with chronic kidney disease (estimated glomerular filtration rate [eGFR], 30 to 90 ml per minute per 1.73 m At baseline, the urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio was similar among the participants in the three groups; the median value was 579 (interquartile range, 292 to 1092) among those with available data (265 in the combination-therapy group, 258 in the finerenone group, and 261 participants in the empagliflozin group)."^^xsd:string ;
        oe:cites oesrc:40327845,
            oesrc:40450519,
            oesrc:40470996,
            oesrc:40935879 ;
        oe:questionText "What is the recommended first-line pharmacological treatment for Diabetic Nephropathy?"^^xsd:string .

    oedrug:lisinopril oe:treats oed:diabetic_nephropathy .
}

