    oeq:q_bipolar_disorder_treatment oe:answerText "Medication management in women with bipolar disorder (BD) in the perinatal period is challenging, given that many patients taper or stop medication during pregnancy, and the postpartum period is an extremely high-risk period for relapse. The objective of this narrative review was to investigate the perinatal efficacy as well as potential adverse effects on the child of common treatments for bipolar disorder."^^xsd:string ;
