    oeq:q_osteoporosis_efficacy oe:answerText "Zoledronate prevents fractures in older women when administered every 12 to 18 months, but its effects on bone density and bone turnover persist beyond 5 years. Whether infrequent zoledronate administration would prevent vertebral fractures in early postmenopausal women is unknown."^^xsd:string ;
        oe:cites oesrc:36920813,
            oesrc:37991856,
            oesrc:38691368,
            oesrc:39813642 ;
        oe:questionText "How effective is prednisone compared with other agents for Osteoporosis?"^^xsd:string .

